  "section_notes": "The final rules are strong on reporting (24h/72h), testing (55°C, 5% benchmark, customer and regulator results, no public publication), remote shut-off (new units and 6-year retrofit), fire suppression (36 months), and recall (8/100k mandatory with prompt notice). All four red lines are respected, and the main compromises are the six-year retrofit, 36-month suppression, and corrective-action pathway for S2 rather than automatic market exclusion. S2 and S5 have no phase-in periods, and S5 lacks an explicit serious-injury recall clause."
